 "summary": "Python-only conventions step for all 488 GT23 recordings: pelvis (PSIS-ASIS markers), thigh and shank (authors model axes from Transforms_Euler), foot (heel to toe markers) segment angles in the pelvis-heading plane; joint angles as differences; joint speeds recomputed by central difference (no smoothing); pressure point in the foot frame (origin 100 mm forward of the ankle-marker midpoint); lab-axis force everywhere plus forward/sideways force in the 11 forward-walking tasks only. 6 pilots + 12 batches + 1 summary under the guarded launcher, one at a time. Independent verifier NOT yet run.",
 "decisions_applied": [
  "D-GT23-C01-1 = C (forward/sideways force only in 11 forward-walking tasks; lab axes elsewhere)",
  "D-REF-1/2 (23 Nov 2026): joint angles = differences of gravity-referenced segment angles; pressure point in the foot frame",
  "knee flexion positive (standard)",
  "plan defaults G1-G5, with G5 changed per the task brief: speeds recomputed from new angles, published speeds/powers kept only as a recorded comparison"
 ],
 "module": "contributor_tools/gt23_conventions.py (pure maths), contributor_tools/gt23_conventions_check.py (second independent implementation: scalar loops, scipy Rotation YZX, Gram-Schmidt basis, complex-number angles), contributor_tools/run_gt23_c06.py (run, spec, summary)",
