 "columns_per_recording_parquet": "time_s; pelvis_sagittal_angle_rad; {thigh,shank,foot}_sagittal_angle_{left,right}_rad; {hip_flexion,knee_flexion,ankle_dorsiflexion}_angle_{left,right}_rad and _velocity_{left,right}_rad_s; cop_{anterior,vertical,lateral}_{left,right}_m (foot frame); grf_lab_{x,y,z}_{left,right}_N and cop_lab_{x,z}_{left,right}_m (lab axes, loaded >=20 N only for the pressure point); grf_{anterior,lateral}_{left,right}_N and heading_lab_{x,z}_{left,right} (11 forward tasks only). Force stays in N here; body-weight scaling is M01.",
 "method_notes": [
  "Lab frame: +Y up, markers mm->m. Forward = up x (right ASIS - left ASIS) per sample (plan G4); right = forward x up.",
  "Euler tables: intrinsic Y-Z-X, columns in file order (not their names), body-to-lab; verified on AB05 against markers (tibia/femur y axis along the bone, calcaneus x along heel-to-toe, pelvis x forward).",
  "Pelvis angle = marker PSIS-mid to ASIS-mid; thigh/shank = Transforms_Euler body y axis (proximal to distal); foot = CAL to mean(MT1,MT5). Joint angles are differences, no other zero. Composition max abs error over all 488 recordings 4.4e-16 rad.",
  "Speeds: central difference of the new angle (wrapped), 200 Hz, no smoothing; NaN at gaps and ends.",
  "Pressure point: 3-D foot frame (anterior = heel-to-toe, up = vertical with its heel-to-toe part removed, no roll; lateral outward). Origin 100 mm forward of the midpoint of the two ankle markers. Plate vertical force < 20 N or missing -> pressure point NaN (zero lab COP is not a measurement). Foot-frame pressure point is computed in ALL tasks because the foot frame does not need a walking direction; the older acceptance line \"pressure point empty in the 15 no-forward tasks\" predates D-REF-2 (23 Nov) and is superseded by the standard.",
  "Forward/sideways force: heading held fixed per S01 stride/window span of that leg (side L/R or both), whole recording for continuous start_stop; loaded samples not covered by any span (stairs single contacts, uncovered window samples) take the mean heading of their own contact (recorded per recording: heading_from_contact_when_no_span). Empty in the 15 no-forward tasks.",
  "Model geometry (re-implemented from the .osim text, not imported): hip centre, ankle/talus centre via tibia markers and via calcaneus marker, used only as cross-checks. Models: AB01 -Scaled1_original, others -Scaled1 (hash-checked against the X01 participant file). AB03 model has no ASIS markers so its model hip-centre/thigh cross-check is unavailable (recorded).",
  "Markers actually used in the primary columns: ASIS/PSIS, heel, MT1, MT5, ankle pair (pressure point only). Thigh clusters, knee markers and trochanters are not used, so the 3 AB03 stair recordings missing RTHC and AB13 stairs_1_9 missing RKNE hold no column."
 ],
