 "findings_odd": [
  "Pelvis: marker pelvis angle and the model pelvis tilt correlate r 0.78-0.98 per participant over whole recordings (residual sd 0.9-2.1 deg), not near 0 as the plan probe found; the constant offset per participant (-16.3 to +0.3 deg) matches the model own PSIS-ASIS landmark angle within a few degrees. Hip offsets against the publisher equal minus that pelvis offset. No IK reference exists for the PSIS-ASIS definition; the model landmark angle is the reference used.",
  "Foot/ankle: marker foot angle differs from the model calcaneus x axis by a per-subject constant that follows the model heel/toe landmark angle; this is the ankle offset against the publisher (AB07 about -9 to -13 deg is the largest).",
  "Ankle moment slope published/computed: AB03 1.43 and AB08 1.3 fit the known C05 mass issue (published per-kg moment used another mass); the other participants are 0.65 to 1.17 (AB05 0.65 is pulled down by non-walking tasks; AB05 turn_and_step pilot 0.66).",
  "Walking-only ankle speed sign agreement is 0.9 to 0.97 (marker-derived ankle noise, rms difference about 17% of published rms).",
  "Treadmill plates: right plate force is missing in 408 of the held plate columns; no right-leg pressure point exists for those recordings.",
  "Stairs pressure point fixed (outside share 62% -> 0.7%, moment ratio 0.35 -> 1.09). Curb_up pressure point held (see rework_after_first_review)."
 ],
