  "bug": "pressure point used plate height 0; source COPY_Vertical (stairs 0.35-0.83 m, incline treadmill small nonzero, curb 0.009 m) is now used wherever finite (cv.plate_point); unknown height or load < 20 N gives NaN. Raised-plate synthetic test added.",
  "curb_up": "AB03 curb_up_1 and all curb_up recordings: the recorded plate height is 0.009 m but the heel marker is 0.20-0.23 m above it while loaded (foot on a curb of undocumented height). Foot-frame pressure point (anterior, vertical, lateral) is HELD for those 24 leg-recordings with a reason (rule: median heel height above plate > 0.17 m; diagnostic over curb, cutting, step_ups, tire_run and stairs showed 0.05-0.146 m for every other leg-recording and 0.200-0.229 m for every curb_up one). Lab-axis force and plate COP are kept.",
  "cutting_step_ups_curb_down": "not held. Residual outside-foot share 10-15% (cutting 15%, step_ups 12.5%, curb_down 10%) also exists in level walking (12%) and is a property of the 5 cm margin around heel and MT-head markers (marker foot length 0.20 m, real foot longer) plus low-load edges: in AB05 normal_walk 10% outside even at >= 0.2 BW, 51% below it; cutting 23% / 69%. Ankle-moment ratio 1.04-1.12 with r 0.99 supports the values.",
